1 NAME Alexander* Heinrich /Eggers/
2 GIVN Alexander* Heinrich
2 SURN Eggers
2 _MARNM Eggers
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 3 APR 1867
2 PLAC Reval (Tallinn), Harjumaa, Estland 
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 13 JUN 1937
2 PLAC Berlin-Karlshorst, Germany 
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Pädagoge und Publizist 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Schoolteacher, a former Student of Indology. Son of businessman Alexander E. (1828–1877) and Marie Hiekisch. Educated at Government Gymnasium in Reval (Tallinn) 1880-85. From 1885 studies of medicine and in 1886-91
2 CONC  of Comparative Grammar at Dorpat (under Leo Meyer and L. von Schroeder). In 1891 cand. and 1894 mag.philol. (Ph.D.) at Dorpat (Tartu). Then in 1896-1906 teacher (Oberlehrer of German language) and 1906-10 director at Domschule in
2 CONC  Reval, 1910-14 Schulrat and Oberlehrer ibid. In 1915 moved to Sweden, 1916-18 author in Berlin, 1918 Stadtschulrat in Reval, In 1919-28 director of Privatlyzeum in Greifswald. From 1928 Studienrat at Zemkessches Privatlyzeum in B
2 CONC erlin. Married 1903 his cousin Clara Eggers, children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Publications: Diss. Der arische (indo-iranische) Gott Mitra. Eine sprach- und religionsgeschichtliche Studie. 92 p. Dorpat 1894.
2 CONT
2 CONT – Further writings on pedagogics; edited Baltische Briefe aus zwei Jahrhunderten. 283 p. 1918 and Baltische Lebenserinnerungen. 348 p. Heilbronn 1926.
2 CONT
