1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT <strong>Parry, Sir William Edward</strong>. 19/12/1790-08/07/1855. Ref: 1186. Male.
2 CONT * Titles and British Honours: Rear Admiral(1852), Knight(1829).
2 CONT * Place of Birth: Bath, Somerset.
2 CONT * Place of Death: Ems, Germany.
2 CONT * Place of interment: Burial-ground of Greenwich Hospital.
2 CONT * Profession: Royal Navy, Arctic Explorer.
2 CONT * Appointments Held: 1802 enlisted RN, Lieutenant 1810, Commanded expeditions to North-West Passage 1819-20, 1821-3, 1824-5, Hydrographer 1825-9, Admiralty; Manager 1829-34 Australian Company; Captain-Superintendent 1847-Haslar Ho
2 CONC spital; Lt-Governor 1853, Greenwich Hospital.
2 CONT * Schools and Tutors: Bath Grammar School.
2 CONT * Postgraduate Studies: DCL (Oxon 1829).
2 CONT * Marital Status: Married (1826) Hon. Isabella Louisa Stanley d. 1839, 2nd (1841) Catherine Edwards Hawkinson,(Mrs Hoare).
2 CONT * Mother: Nee Rigby.
2 CONT * Father: Dr Caleb Hillier Parry 1755-1822.
2 CONT * References: DNB 43, 1895, 392-3; Proc Roy Soc, 7, 1856, 603-12; Poggendorff 2, 367.
2 CONT * Memberships: FRS (1821), MWS.
2 CONT * Date of Election: 17/03/1845.
2 CONT * Proposers: Proposed by Council as Honorary British Fellow (Council Minute 17/01/1845 NLS Acc10,000/18).
2 CONT * Fellow Type: HF.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Waterston, Charles D; Macmillan Shearer, A (July 2006). [http://www.royalsoced.org.uk/cms/files/fellows/biographical_index/fells_indexp2.pdf Biographical index of former fellows of the Royal Society of Edinburgh, 1783-200
2 CONC 2]: Biographical Index. II. Edinburgh: The Royal Society of Edinburgh. ISBN 978-0-902198-84-5. page 717
2 CONT
