2 ADDR
3 CITY Leonberg
3 STAE Württemberg
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE 3 JAN 1864
1 OCCU Pastor in Saratow
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.norkarussia.info/christian-gottlieb-hegele.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian Gottlieb Hegele was born in Hirschlanden, Leonberg, Württemberg on June 24, 1804. In 1923, Hegele began his theological training at the Mission Institute in Basel, Switzerland (membership number 68). After completion of 
2 CONC his training in Basel, he served as pastor in the Volga German colony of Beideck from 1836 to 1850 and in Yagodnaya-Polyana from 1850 until his death there on January 3, 1864. While serving as pastor of the Beideck parish, Hegele 
2 CONC also served Norka from 1841 to 1845, during a period of time when the colony did not have a resident pastor. Hegele married Nancy Galloway, the daughter of James Galloway who served in Karras (North Caucasus) with the Scottish Mis
2 CONC sion Society, and sister to the wife of Pastor Karl Heinrich Thomas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two of Hegele's sisters married missionaries from the Mission Institute in Basel (Jakob Lang and Johann Theodore Wolters).
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.norka-russland.net/christian-gottlieb-hegele.html
