1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Garnier
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Garnier (1776–1873) was an English churchman and botanist, Dean of Winchester from 1840 to 1872.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was educated at Hyde Abbey School and Worcester College, Oxford. He was appointed Rector of Bishopstoke, Hampshire, in 1807.
2 CONT
2 CONT Whilst Dean, he was a founding member of the Hampshire Horticultural Society in 1818 (Dean Garnier's Garden in Winchester's cathedral close is named after him) and, in the 1860s, an 'anti-muckabite' campaigner for a sewerage syste
2 CONC m for Winchester (with the road to the town's first sewerage pumping station later being named after him).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a friend of Palmerston and a staunch whig.
2 CONT
