1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''From [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_Parry_%28Bishop_of_Dover%29 Wikipedia: Edward Parry (bishop of Dover)]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Parry (Thursday, 14 January 1830 – Friday, 11 April 1890) was a Bishop of Dover.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parry was the son of William Parry, Arctic explorer, and Isabella Louisa Stanley, his wife, fourth daughter of the John Stanley, 1st Baron Stanley of Alderley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parry was educated at [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rugby_School Rugby School, Lawrence Sheriff Street, Rugby, Warwickshire CV22 5EH 52.3675, -1.2611] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balliol_College,_Oxford Balliol College, Br
2 CONC oad Street, Oxford OX1 3BJ 51.7547, -1.2578] and began his ordained ministry as a curate in Norham. After time as chaplain to the Bishop of London, Archibald Campbell Tait, he became Rural Dean of Ealing. In 1869 he was appointed 
2 CONC Archdeacon of Canterbury and on the Feast of the Annunciation, Friday, 25 March 1870, was consecrated at Lambeth Palace chapel ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_Museum St Mary-at-Lambeth, now Garden Museum, 5 Lambeth Palace R
2 CONC oad, Lambeth, London SE1 7LB 51.4950, -0.1202]) the fourth Bishop of Dover (suffragan bishop in the Diocese of Canterbury), 273 years after the death of the third bishop. A monument to him is in Canterbury Cathedral. In 1882 he wa
2 CONC s chosen by the Australian bishops to succeed the late Frederic Barker as Bishop of Sydney and Metropolitan of Australia, but he declined the nomination.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parry's sons, Edward Parry and Sydney Parry were, respectively, Bishop of Guyana (1900–1921) and Archbishop of the West Indies (1917–1921), and a senior British civil servant. Sydney Parry wrote the article about his father in the
2 CONC  Dictionary of National Biography. Another son was Admiral Sir John Franklin Parry, Hydrographer of the Navy during the First World War.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=TaUThWfDW4RFdQbMnP1ceg&scan=1 FreeBMD: Registration of marriage of Edward Parry in 1859] and [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=giAgaus5AXOvsDHOhvbcCQ&sc
2 CONC an=1 FreeBMD: Registration of marriage of Matilda Williams in 1859]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * April to June 1859: Registration of marriage of Matilda Williams; in St. James (Volume 1a, Page 642)
2 CONT * April to June 1859: Registration of marriage of Edward Parry; in St James (Volume 1a, Page 642)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Author of [https://idiscover.lib.cam.ac.uk/permalink/f/t9gok8/44CAM_ALMA21274035480003606 Memorials of Charles Parry, Commander, Royal Navy, by his brother Edward Parry, Suffragan Bishop of Dover Published 1879]'''
2 CONT
