2 CONT '''From [https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0000270/18911010/036/0007 British Newspaper Archive: Bucks Herald Saturday, 10 October 1891 Page 7 Swanbourne]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage of Mr. F. S. Parry and Miss A. M. Fremantle. — On Thursday afternoon, 1 October 1891, at [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canterbury_Cathedral Canterbury Cathedral, The Precincts, Canterbury, Kent CT1 2EH 51.279722, 1.08305
2 CONC 6], the wedding took place of Mr. Frederick Sydney Parry, second son of the late Bishop of Dover, and Miss Anna Mary Fremantle, youngest daughter of the Rev. the Hon. W. H. Fremantle, Canon of Canterbury, and fellow of Balliol Col
2 CONC lege, Oxford. The service was conducted by the Dean of Ripon, great uncle of the bride, the Dean of Canterbury, the Rev. the Hon. W. H. Fremantle, and the Rev. P. A. Parry, rector of Sundridge, brother of the bridegroom.
2 CONT
2 CONT The bridesmaids were Miss Isabella L. Fremantle, sister of the bride, Miss Isabel Bertha Parry, sister of the bridegroom, Miss Margaret Fremantle, Miss Laura Carr, cousin of the bride, and Miss Maude Ward, cousin of the bridegroom
2 CONC . There were also two pages. The bride was given away by her father. The Hon. T. F. Fremantle was best man.
2 CONT
2 CONT Among these present were Lord and Lady Cottesloe and the Hon. Mary Fremantle, Hon. Sir Charles and Lady Fremantle, Admiral Hon. Sir Edmund and Lady Fremantle, Viscount and Viscountess Midleton and Hon. Albinia Brodrick, the Dean o
2 CONC f Ripon and Mrs. Fremantle, etc.
2 CONT
