2 CONT 19 June 1921 Census: 9 people living in 63 Elm Park Gardens, Chelsea, London, England; House with 17 rooms
2 CONT * Frederick Sydney Parry, head, male, married; aged 60 years 0 months [born about 1861] in Acton, Middlesex; Deputy Chairman H M Customs and Excise at Custom House, London EC3
2 CONT * Anna Mary Parry, wife, female, married; aged 53 years 11 months [born about 1867] in London, Middlesex; Home Duties and Girls' Club Organiser (Unpaid); at Home and at Girls' Friendly Society, London Diocese
2 CONT * William Edward Parry, son, male, single; aged 28 years 2 months [born about 1893] in London, Middlesex; Lieutenant Royal Navy
2 CONT * Katherine Isabel Parry, daughter, female, single; aged 26 years 6 months [born about 1895] in London, Middlesex; Health Visitor (Student); Ministry of Health at Battersea Polytechnic
2 CONT * Maudelleay[?] Dayles Hazetton, visitor, female, divorced with 0 young children; aged 27 years 0 months [born about 1894] in Meerut, India, resident, British born; Dealer in Antiques; [Duer?] Euan Thomas Antiques at 20 Dover Stre
2 CONC et, London W
2 CONT * Hilda Kate Clarke, servant, female, single; aged 28 years 3 months [born about 1893] in Cromer Hyde, Hertfordshire; Housekeeper; Private
2 CONT * Ida Rosetta Dorling, servant, female, single; aged 27 years 10 months [born about 1893] in Great Ashfield, Suffolk; Cook; Private
2 CONT * Mary Bowers, servant, female, single; aged 23 years 11 months [born about 1897] in Great Wratting, Suffolk; Parlourmaid; Private
2 CONT * Winifred Maud Burchell, servant, female, single; aged 22 years 5 months [born about 1899] in Reading, Berkshire; Housemaid; Private
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-10678-13777115/frederick-s-parry-in-1939-register-of-england-wales MyHeritage: Frederick S Parry: 1939 Register of England & Wales (transcription only)]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 29 September 1939 Census for residents of [https://britishlistedbuildings.co.uk/101194393-hooke-hall-uckfield Hooke Hall, 250 High Street, Uckfield, East Sussex TN22 1EN 50.9743, 0.0985], England
2 CONT * Frederick S Parry, head, married, male, aged 78, born Wednesday, 5 June 1861; Home Civil Service (Retired)
2 CONT * Anna M Parry, wife (implied), married, female, aged 72, born Sunday, 7 July 1867; Unpaid Domestic Duties
2 CONT * Mary K Potter, married, female, aged 29, born Thursday, 4 August 1910; Cook
2 CONT * Florence A Dennell (Jones), single, female, aged 32, born Wednesday, 29 May 1907; House Parlourmaid
2 CONT * Sydney V Yorke, single, male, aged 43, born Monday, 27 April 1896; School Master
2 CONT * Peter G Robinson, single, male, aged 16, born Friday, 19 October 1923; At School
2 CONT * Howard G F Bartlett, single, male, aged 15, born Thursday, 11 December 1924; At School
2 CONT * Henry B Peachey, single, male, aged 16, born Thursday, 25 October 1923; At School
2 CONT * John R Steptoe, single, male, aged 14, born Tuesday, 3 February 1925; At School
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=uInwSF5L05ns%2Fa99mz15ww&scan=1 FreeBMD - Registration of death of Frederick S Parry in 1941]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT April to June 1941: Registration of death of Frederick S Parry; aged 79 [born about 1862]; in Hove (Volume 2b, Page 684)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0000483/19410530/155/0006 British Newspaper Archive: Kent & Sussex Courier Friday, 30 May 1941 Page 6 Late Sir Sydney Parry]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT A large and representative congregation attended the funeral service at [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Margaret_the_Queen,_Buxted St Margaret the Queen, Buxted, East Sussex TN22 4AY 50.987606, 0.115783], on Saturday, 24 May 194
2 CONC 1 for Sir Frederick Sydney Parry, Uckfield, who died at Hove on Thursday week, 22 May 1941.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father of Commodore W. E. Parry, of H.M.S. Achilles, and in 1885 became Assistant Private Secretary to the Chancellor of the Exchequer. From 1897 to 1902 he was Private Secretary to the First Lord of the Treasury.
2 CONT
2 CONT The service was conducted by Canon K. H. MacDermott and the Rt. Rev. C. J. G. Saunders, and the family mourners were Lady Parry, Mr. Peter Parry, Miss Ann Parry, the Rev. E. L. Ridge, Mrs. Ridge, Miss Ridge, Miss A. Ridge, Miss Al
2 CONC ison Aitkin, Prebendary C. H. Way, Miss Mersia Hardcastle, (representing Archdeacon Hardcastle. Mrs. Hamond, the Misses W. and M Hardcastle, Sir Francis Fremantle, M.P., and Lady Fremantle, the Hon. Reginald and Mrs. Fremantle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Others present included Brigadier-General E. O'Brien C.B., Miss B. Williams, Capt. and Mrs. Stanmer, Mr. O'Grady, Miss May, Mr. and Mrs. S. Tooth, Miss Helena Jenkenson, Mr. H. A. Fleming, Mr. and Mrs. H. Barrow, Miss Beard, D. A.
2 CONC  Ware, Mrs. May, Mr. C. G. D. Hoare, Miss Hoare, Miss Lynn, Miss D. Lynn, Mr. and Mrs. E. J. Grainger, Mr. H. W. Wilde, Mr. L. Wilde, Mrs. Stenning (representing Uckfield Mothers' Union), Major-General Sir Hugh Bruce-Williams, K.C
2 CONC .B., Dr. and Mrs. C. Williams, Miss Williams, Mrs. Tuohy, Mrs. Philip Morten, Mrs. Hockey, Mrs. A. K. Hobart-Hampden, Mrs. Bates, Miss Ware, Mr. and Mrs. Cyrus Braby, Mr. E. J. McGillivray, Mr. J. H. Newman, Mrs. Scarlett, Mrs. Gl
2 CONC encairn Campbell, Mrs. Saunders, Rev. F. J. W. Taverner, Lieut.-Colonel E. C. Lentaigne, D.S.O., and Mrs. Lentaigne, Mrs. C. Kenward, Miss Livingstone, Miss Callis, Rev. J. H. Gurney. Prebendary Parry Way and Mrs. Lambert.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.ancestry.co.uk/imageviewer/collections/1904/images/32858_609838_2422-00111 Ancestry 19410815 probate Sir Frederick Sydney Parry KBE CB Hooke Hall Uckfield Sussex d 194105227 Wilbury Road Hove pr Llandudno Kate
2 CONC  Julia Parry widow £4648]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 August 1941 probate of Sir Frederick Sydney Parry K.B.E., C.B., of Hooke Hall, Uckfield, Sussex, who died 22 May 1941, at [7 Wilbury Road, Hove, Sussex BN3 3GJ 50.8285442, -0.1667879], probate granted at Llandudno on 15 August 
2 CONC 1941 to Kate Julia Parry, widow. Effects £4648 8s. 11d. Resworn £4331 16s. 7d.
