2 CONT
2 CONT Adm. pens. at ST JOHN'S College, 4 Oct 1889. <br/>
2 CONT [Youngest] s. of the Rev. John Hugh (Oriel College, Oxford, 1853), Vicar of Henbury, Gloucs. (and Caroline, dau. of Admiral Sir W. Edward Parry, K.C.B., the Arctic explorer). <br/>
2 CONT Born 10 Jan 1870, at Henbury Vicarage. <br/>
2 CONT School, Repton. <br/>
2 CONT Matric. Michs. 1889; B.A. 1892; M.A. 1901. <br/>
2 CONT Ordained deacon (Lichfield) 1894; priest, 1895; <br/>
2 CONT Curate of St Peter's, Wolverhampton, 1894-1903. Curate of Basford, Staffs., 1903-6. Vicar of Henbury with Aust and Hallen, Gloucs., 1906-28. Honorary Canon of Bristol, 1926-8. Vicar of Chesterton with Alsager Banks, Staffs., 1928-
2 CONC 30. Rector of St Chad's, Lichfield, 1930-3. Vicar of Eccleshall, 1933-9. Prebendary of Lichfield, 1939. Rector of Denham, Bucks., 1939-46. <br/>
2 CONT Married, 27 Apr 1905, Ethel Mary, eldest dau. of Joseph Walker Danks, of Wolverhampton, and had issue. <br/>
2 CONT Latterly of Denham Lodge, Eccleshall, Staffs., where he died Nov. 30, 1949. <br/>
2 CONT (Crockford; Who's Who; Burke, L.G.; The Times, Apr. 29, 1905 and Dec. 2, 1949; Church Times, Dec. 9, 1949.)
