3 CITY London
3 CTRY England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 23 DEC 1928
2 ADDR
3 CITY Witcombe
3 STAE England
3 CTRY England
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT <strong>Dyer, Sir William Turner Thiselton-</strong>. 28/07/1843-23/12/1928. Ref: 2471. Male.
2 CONT * Titles and British Honours: CMG (1882), CIE (1892), KCMG(1899).
2 CONT * Place of Birth: Westminster, London.
2 CONT * Place of Death: Witcombe, Gloucestershire.
2 CONT * Profession: Botanist.
2 CONT * Appointments Held: Professor 1868-70, Royal Agricultural College, Cirencester; 1870-2 Botany, Royal College of Science, Dublin; 1872-5 Botany, Royal Horticultural Society; Assistant Director 1875-85, Director 1885-1905, Royal Bo
2 CONC tanic Garden, Kew.
2 CONT * Schools and Tutors: King's College School, London.
2 CONT * Undergraduate Studies: MA (Oxon,), B Sc(London 1869).
2 CONT * Postgraduate Studies: LL.D.
2 CONT * Marital Status: Married (1877) Harriet Ann Hooker.
2 CONT * Mother: Catherine Jane Firminger.
2 CONT * Father: William George Thiselton Dyer, physician in Westminster.
2 CONT * Other Family: Son-in-law of Sir Joseph Dalton Hooker FRSE 1817-1911.
2 CONT * References: DNB 1922-1930, 1937, 830-2; Proc Roy Soc B106, 1930.xxiii-xxix signed FWO; Proc Roy Soc Edinb, 49, 1928-29, 377; Who Was Who 2.
2 CONT * Memberships: FRS (1880).
2 CONT * Date of Election: 03/11/1913.
2 CONT * Proposers: Proposed by Council as Honorary British Fellow (Billet 7/7, 21/7/1913).
2 CONT * Fellow Type: HF.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Waterston, Charles D; Macmillan Shearer, A (July 2006). [http://www.royalsoced.org.uk/cms/files/fellows/biographical_index/fells_indexp1.pdf Biographical index of former fellows of the Royal Society of Edinburgh, 1783-200
2 CONC 2]: Biographical Index. I. Edinburgh: The Royal Society of Edinburgh. ISBN 978-0-902198-84-5. page 283
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
