1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Colonel William Kaye Legge was born on 13 June 1869.1 He was the son of Hon. Charles Gounter Legge and Mary Garnier.1 He married Constance Adeline Palmer, daughter of Hon. James David Palmer, on 9 June 1902.1 He di
2 CONC ed on 29 March 1946 at age 76.1
2 CONT
2 CONT      Colonel William Kaye Legge fought in the Boer War between 1899 and 1902, where he was mentioned in despatches.1 He fought in the First World War, where he was mentioned in despatches.1 He gained the rank of Colonel in the ser
2 CONC vice of the Essex Regiment.1 He was decorated with the Companion, Distinguished Service Order (D.S.O.) in 1917.1 He was invested as a Companion, Order of St. Michael and St. George (C.M.G.) in 1918.1 He was decorated with the Croi
2 CONC x de Guerre.1 He gained the rank of Honorary Brigadier-General in 1926.1
