2 CONC 6], the wedding took place of Mr. Frederick Sydney Parry, second son of the late Bishop of Dover, and Miss Anna Mary Fremantle, youngest daughter of the Rev. the Hon. W. H. Fremantle, Canon of Canterbury, and fellow of [https://en
2 CONC .wikipedia.org/wiki/Balliol_College,_Oxford Balliol College, Broad Street, Oxford OX1 3BJ 51.7547, -1.2578]. The service was conducted by the Dean of Ripon, great uncle of the bride, the Dean of Canterbury, the Rev. the Hon. W. H.
2 CONC  Fremantle, and the Rev. P. A. Parry, rector of Sundridge, brother of the bridegroom.
2 CONT
2 CONT The bridesmaids were Miss Isabella L. Fremantle, sister of the bride, Miss Isabel Bertha Parry, sister of the bridegroom, Miss Margaret Fremantle, Miss Laura Carr, cousin of the bride, and Miss Maude Ward, cousin of the bridegroom
2 CONC . There were also two pages. The bride was given away by her father. The Hon. T. F. Fremantle was best man.
2 CONT
2 CONT Among these present were Lord and Lady Cottesloe and the Hon. Mary Fremantle, Hon. Sir Charles and Lady Fremantle, Admiral Hon. Sir Edmund and Lady Fremantle, Viscount and Viscountess Midleton and Hon. Albinia Brodrick, the Dean o
2 CONC f Ripon and Mrs. Fremantle, etc.
