1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jacob Friedrich von Steinheil (1717-1800) distinguished himself in the military. He served as a volunteer in the Russian army and took part in the siege of Ochakov in 1737, where he was wounded thrice. He subsequen
2 CONC tly left the service and went home with his brother, Johann Wilhelm. In 1743, he returned to Russia, where he was enrolled in the Nizovsky Infantry Regiment; he rose to the rank of lieutenant. After retiring, he settled in the Est
2 CONC land Governorate, taking up agriculture and managing several estates.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann Wilhelm and Jacob Friedrich were the first Steingels to move to Estonia for permanent residence.
