1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NASHVILLE, TENN./OREGON-Trond Sandvik, age 79, passed away on Tuesday, Dec. 21, 2010 at HospiceCare Inc. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born on Aug. 13, 1931 in Namsos, Norway, the son of Joel and Magna (Aune) Sandvik. Trond taught Art History for several universities in Kentucky before moving on to become the Arts and Education Director at Cheekwood Museum
2 CONC  in Nashville, Tenn. In addition, he had an art perspectives radio program, on public radio station WPLN, in which he would discuss art interpretation throughout the United States. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Trond enjoyed cooking for friends and the holidays and built on that enjoyment by having his own catering business for several years. He enjoyed traveling to review art, loved reading and all sorts of word play. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Trond is survived by his children, Martin (Jo) Sandvik, Christine (Steve) Johnston and their mother, Karin Sandvik; grandchildren, Evan and Taylor Johnston; special friends, Gary Pace and Lin Folk. 
