0 @N6000000003216046140@ NOTE Attended St Helen's School. Pembroke Road, Dublin at the same time as his brother Billy.  Won Form III prize in 1897.
1 CONT 1905-6 RMA Woolwich.  Promoted 2nd Lt Jan 1907 and gazetted to 51st Battery Royal Field Artillery at Shorncliffe,  part of 39th Bde RFA.  Photographed at Piershill Barracks, Edinburgh in 1909.
1 CONT Promoted Lieutenant 20 Dec 1909.  Sailed with his Regiment from Southampton 21 Nov 1913 on the MHT Dongola, arriving in Karachi 13 Dec 1913.  Promoted Captain 30 Oct 1914.  Wounded in India in 1916.  Serving in Risalpur, India at 
1 CONC Christmas 1916 with M Battery Royal Regiment of Artillery.  Promoted Acting Major 8 Apr 1917 (26 Jan 1917, according to L Gazette dated 18 May 1917).  Ordered back to England Aug 1917 after four years service overseas.  Served in 
1 CONC Germany in 1918 - 1919 with the 16th Brigade RHA.  Decorated during WW1 (War Office: Service Medal and Award Rolls Index, First World War Ref WO 372/1).  Mentioned in a despatch from Field Marshall Sir Douglas Haig, dated 16 Mar 1
1 CONC 919, for gallant and distinguished services in the Field.  Part of the Inter-Allied Commission of Control in 1921.  Appointed Brigade Major, Divisional RA, 53rd Welsh Division , TA in Mar 1922.  Served in WWII.  Placed on the Half
1 CONC -pay List 1 Apr 1939, after 4 years' service as Regimental Lt-Col of Field Branch RRA. (L Gazette 31 Mar 1939).  Retired on retired pay 1 Oct 1939 (L Gazette 3 Oct 1939).  Ceased to belong to the Reserve of Officers 13 Jan 1945 (L
1 CONC  Gazette Supp. 12 Jan 1945).
0 @N6000000003216049021@ NOTE Entered Royal Naval College, Osborne May 1909.  At Dartmouth 1912-13, passing out 13th of 62.
1 CONT Appointed to HMS Cornwall May to Nov 1913, HMS Temeraire 18,600 tons, 23,000 HP, 10x12" 16x4" and 4x3 Pounder guns, based at Devonport, 15 Jan 1914.  Awarded three months seniority and promoted Midshipman 15 Jan 1914.
1 CONT Joined HMS Savage, a Portsmouth-basedTorpedo Boat Destroyer on 1 Mar 1916 as acting Sub-Lieutenant.  Promoted Acting Lieutenant on 15 Oct 1916 and confirmed Lieutenant on 15 Jan 1918.  Joined HMS Dolphin on 18 August 1818 "for sub
1 CONC marines".  Served with the 7th s/m Flotilla in Baltic in 1919.  Appointed to ML550 in Command, to date 23 Sep 1919.  Joined HMS Royal Oak in January 1920  and visited Constantinople.  March 1922 appointed to HMS Excellent for Long
1 CONC  Gunnery Course.
1 CONT
1 CONT Served as Acting Captain (whilst a Cdr Retired) during WWII.  Staff Captain to Flag Officer Western Mediterranean. DSC 4 May 1943 (Operation Torch).  Placed on Retd List with rank of Commander 29 Jul 1941 (L Gazette 8 Aug 1941).
1 CONT Education: RN Colleges, Osborne (1909-1912) & Dartmouth (1912-1913)
